   "text": "The drawing is Boc-protected threonine: a three-carbon chain with the Boc-NH group on C2, a hydroxyl on C3, a methyl on C3 and a carboxylic acid on C2.\n\n**Connectivity:**\n- The alpha carbon carries NH\u2013Boc, the CO2H group and the beta carbon.\n- The beta carbon carries OH, the CH3 and the alpha carbon.\n- Boc expands to C(=O)OC(C)(C)C, attached through the carbamate carbon to N.\n\n**Stereochemistry:** the wedges are on the CO2H bond (alpha carbon) and the CH3 bond (beta carbon). The implicit hydrogen on each stereocentre points away from the viewer.\n- Alpha carbon: the priorities are N > CO2H > CB. Viewed from the front, N \u2192 CB \u2192 CO2H runs clockwise, so N \u2192 CO2H \u2192 CB runs counterclockwise, giving S.\n- Beta carbon: the priorities are OH > C\u03b1 > CH3. Going OH \u2192 C\u03b1 \u2192 CH3 runs clockwise, giving R.\n\nThis is the (2S,3R) configuration, as in L-threonine. The SMILES below is L-threonine written with the Boc group on nitrogen, with the neighbour order unchanged so the chirality tags carry over.\n\nSMILES: C[C@@H](O)[C@H](NC(=O)OC(C)(C)C)C(=O)O"
